#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Stage 2C: gauge-stable transported-SA3 finite-field response for triplet B2.

Finite-field SA3 eigenvectors are not assigned root by root.  Their complete
three-state frames are aligned to the zero-field (X, A_x, A_y) frame with the
unitary polar factor of the nonorthogonal many-electron overlap matrix.  The
transported Hamiltonian is therefore invariant to finite-field root phases,
permutations, and unitary rotations inside a degenerate subspace.

Stage 1B supplies the audited state-specific zero-field diabatic diagonals;
Stage 2B supplies an independent direct transition-dipole control.  Stage 2C
then obtains diagonal backgrounds, full adiabatic polarizabilities, and
finite-difference quantum metrics from one common finite-field manifold.  At
the exact transverse X/A crossing the lower energy has a |F| cusp, so no
ordinary finite polarizability or finite rank-one metric is reported.
"""

